Asha: TL;DR from postmortem 1: recurring missing spans tied to ETL leader switch + partial commits. We need owners, short timelines, and a safe backfill plan. @Ben @Carla take owners?
Ben: I'll take ETL guard work. Quick plan: (1) require commit_marker visibility before downstream read, (2) add per-shard lag metric, (3) abort partial commit processing. Target: patch in 5 business days, canary next week.
Carla: I'll own aggregator validation + streaming guard. Building small replay harness to assert idempotency and detect duplicated windows. ETA: harness in 2 days, streaming guard follow-up in 4 days. Need temp replay access.
Lina: I'll estimate backfill. Rough: 36-72h run depending on throttle, ~40 node-hours, ~1.5TB temp storage. Cost ~ $900. Will post a runbook and proposed maintenance window by EOW.
Asha: OK. Ops: create tickets and add alerts. Also we want an SLA impact blurb for customers.
ops-bot: Created ticket INFR-4701 "ETL commit visibility check" assigned to Ben, due 2026-04-06. Created ticket INFR-4702 "aggregator replay harness" assigned to Carla, due 2026-04-02.
Ben: Sample patch idea: ```// ensure commit visible before processing
if (!storage.hasCommit(shard, seq)) {
  sleep(50ms);
  if (retry_count > MAX) {
    abortProcessing();
  }
}
```
Carla: Adding alert: span_coverage < 94% over 15m -> page. Also dashboard tile: "span coverage by shard" with 6h trend.
Asha: Recap: Ben 1 ETL guard (due 2026-04-06); Carla 1 aggregator tests + guard (due 2026-04-02); Lina 1 backfill runbook + cost (due 2026-03-31); Asha 1 customer note + maintenance window (due 2026-04-01). Daily check-ins until green.
Carla: Requesting replay credentials in infra channel.
ops-bot: Granted replay creds to Carla until 2026-04-09, provisioned 1 replay node.
Asha: Thanks, will update postmortem doc with action table and start weekly Friday check-ins.
